BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Jack of the Wood
UID:12039@jackofthewood.com
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260910T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260910T213000
DTSTAMP:20260815T143126Z
URL:https://jackofthewood.com/events/bluegrass-jam-special-edition-featuri
 ng-darren-nicholson-the-shed-house-trio-2/
SUMMARY:BLUEGRASS JAM SPECIAL EDITION FEATURING THE DARREN NICHOLSON BAND
DESCRIPTION:\nA Grammy nominee and the winner of 13 International Bluegrass
  Music Association awards\, Darren Nicholson has taken his own brand of mo
 untain music around the world. A regular for years on the Grand Ole Opry a
 nd a founding member of acclaimed bluegrass group Balsam Range\, Darren no
 w spends his time recording\, writing new songs\, and performing original 
 roots music inspired by the history &amp\; culture of his native Western N
 orth Carolina — homegrown\, wholehearted music with a purpose.\n\n\n\nA
  punchy mandolinist with instrumentation nods to Bill Monroe and Marty Stu
 art\, Darren is also an introspective songwriter\, technical harmony singe
 r\, convincing lead vocalist\, and a man on a mission. His shows are a tai
 lored experience — genuine\, entertaining\, and an extended handshake to
  the community.\, reflecting the fun-witted and approachable character for
 med in his raising.\n\n\n\nDarren’s passion is sharing raw\, honest-to-g
 oodness\, quality music with his audience. Music that’s good for his sou
 l and theirs too. “That’s all I want\,” says Darren. “I want to be
  a positive part of other people’s lives with music\, you know? I want t
 o be an ambassador to roots music – tip my hat to the past while looking
  forward at the same time. This music was intended to be played in a way t
 hat adds joy to the community. All I want is to restore that purpose\, not
  to complete a transaction.” \n\n\n\nDarren says that when you come out
  to a show\, whatever you do\, please come talk afterward. “I’m like W
 illie Nelson. ‘I don’t want fans\, I want friends.’ It’s a communa
 l thing.” \n\n\n\nYou can catch Darren almost every week sharing the mu
 sic he loves somewhere\, traveling both nationally and internationally —
  as a solo artist\, in collaboration with other musicians\, and with his o
 wn Darren Nicholson Band — a group of Appalachian musicians with a comm
 on respect for and love of American acoustic music who creatively blend bl
 uegrass\, folk\, gospel\, and swing into a new music experience. \n\n\n\n
 Doors at 6pm —&nbsp\;show starts at 7pm. Suggested cover at the door. Op
 en Jam follows at 9:30pm.\n\n\n\n\nhttps://youtu.be/1WLUcPovyCY?si=aywqVKc
 i4-9xcC3C\n\n\n\n\n\nhttps://youtu.be/ed8sKWA3CCQ?si=rjF1JGqa7dCv61yW\n\n\
 n\n\n\nhttps://youtu.be/8QlDK2gCsLk?si=ZBXy3C8Y2Hjycp0I\n\n\n\n\n\nhttps:/
 /youtu.be/5oUJ-AP-20U?si=l_R6ciyESeMSgy3N\n\n
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://jackofthewood.com/wp-content/uploads/202
 6/05/DarrenNicholson_2025-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Jack of the Wood
UID:12216@jackofthewood.com
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260911T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260911T233000
DTSTAMP:20260819T025530Z
URL:https://jackofthewood.com/events/stacy-antonel/
SUMMARY:Stacy Antonel
DESCRIPTION:\nImagine Tammy Wynette crossed with the Ventures and you’ll 
 have an idea of the sonic world of Americana artist Stacy Antonel’s fort
 hcoming EP\, The Seahorses: Volume 1. Always a genre-defying artist\, Anto
 nel blends her passion for classic country\, jazz and surf rock with this 
 collection of songs\, and the result is a fresh hybrid of musical styles t
 hat feels both vintage and hyper-modern. Recorded at Nashville’s Fitting
  Room Studio\, the band includes heavy hitters Ethan Ballinger (Miranda La
 mbert)\, Joe Reed (Merle Haggard)\, Paul Sgroi (Josh Hedley) and San Diego
  jazz phenom Tony Econom.&nbsp\;\n\n\n\nAntonel grew up in a seaside San D
 iego town called Ocean Beach\, listening to pop and R&amp\;B hits and stud
 ying classical piano until she was eighteen. She cites an eclectic range o
 f artists as her earliest musical inspirations: Tori Amos for her peculiar
  phrasing and distinct songwriting\, Otis Redding for his rich\, emotive v
 ocal delivery. After graduating from UC Berkeley\, she moved to Buenos Air
 es\, where she answered a Craigslist ad for a singer who sounds like June 
 Carter Cash\, and contributed vocals to several jingles for MTV and Jeep t
 hat aired throughout Latin America. She sang in a friend’s electro-cumbi
 a band for a while before returning to California\, where she started sing
 ing professionally at weddings\, bars\, and local venues. But it wasn’t 
 until discovering country music that she felt at home. “One day I random
 ly bought a bunch of 99 cent country records and fell in love with the gen
 re\; the concision of the writing\, the wit\, how it doesn’t take itself
  too seriously even while dealing with deep subject matter.”&nbsp\;\n\n\
 n\nAntonel’s debut album Always the Outsider\, released in 2022\, blends
  elements of mid-century country music with unconventional subject matter 
 and virtuosic instrumentation– including tracks with Doug Pettibone (Luc
 inda Williams) on pedal steel and acoustic guitar. The thematically unique
  collection explores metaphysical and supernatural concepts (alien-earthli
 ng romance\, past-life trauma) as well as grounded narratives of everyday 
 experience (isolation\, disconnectedness\, sexual desire\, feeling like an
  alien in your own body). Always the Outsider was critically praised\, net
 ting coverage in publications from Holler Country to The Bluegrass Situati
 on\, and was hailed as a 2022 Essential Album by Saving Country Music.Musi
 c 8:30-11:30pm $10 cover at the door. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nhttps://youtu.be/G
 pdiE0oeKas?si=byv_F1rpQwSNblb5\n\n\n\n\n\n
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://jackofthewood.com/wp-content/uploads/202
 6/08/stacyantonel1.webp
END:VEVENT
